# Graphics

{% if devbox_software_rendering %}
This machine renders on the CPU. OpenGL comes from Mesa llvmpipe and Vulkan from
lavapipe; both are set up in the environment `agent-env` provides. Expect
correct but slow rendering, and no hardware video encoding.

- Engines and tools that cannot use software Vulkan need their OpenGL path, for
  Unity `-force-glcore`.
- Heavy scenes can take minutes per frame. Lower the resolution before concluding
  that something hangs.
{% else %}
This machine is set to render on its GPU. The virtual desktop uses the first
render node it may open; without a usable one it falls back to an unaccelerated
display, so check before relying on it.
{% endif %}

Check what is in use:

    agent-env glxinfo -B
    agent-env vulkaninfo --summary

A display of your own, for a job that should not show on the shared desktop:

    agent-env xvfb-run -a -s '-screen 0 1280x720x24 +extension GLX' COMMAND ...

The desktop is {{ devbox_geometry }} pixels.
